<title>MEXICO: Bad weather shuts two Mexican crude shipping ports.</title>
<headline>Bad weather shuts two Mexican crude shipping ports.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Two of Mexico's three main crude shipping ports were shut early on Monday because of high wind speeds and waves, authorities at Dos Bocas and Pajaritos ports told Reuters.</p>
<p>The officials said the two ports were unlikely to reopen during the day because wind speeds were increasing.  </p>
<p>Dos Bocas in Tabasco state shut at 0600 local/1200 GMT as waves roared 12 to 14 feet high and wind speeds were 50 to 60 km per hour. Pajaritos in Veracruz state was shut at 0440 local/1040 GMT, with winds at between 50 to 60 km per hour.</p>
<p>A port official at Cayo Arcas in the state of Campeche said the crude exports remained shipping, although winds were expected to reach 60 km later in the day and could possibly shut the port.</p>
<p>((--Timna Tanners, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-7903))</p>
